{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mat-26-1","title":"Matthew 26:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ foretells his own death. 3 The rulers conspire against him. 6 The woman anoints his feet. 14 Judas bargains to betray him. 17 Christ eats the passover; 26 institutes his holy supper; 30 foretells the desertion of his disciples, and Peter's denial; 36 prays in the garden; 47 and being betrayed by a kiss, 57 is carried to Caiaphas, 69 and denied of Peter.</p>\n<p>when. 19:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-26-2","title":"Matthew 26:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>know. Mr 14:1,2; Lu 22:1,2,15; Joh 13:1 the feast. Ex 12:11-14; 34:25; Joh 2:13; 11:55; 12:1 betrayed. 24,25; 17:22; 20:18,19; 27:4; Lu 24:6,7; Joh 13:2; 18:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-26-3","title":"Matthew 26:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>assembled. 21:45,46; Ps 2:1,2; 56:6; 64:4-6; 94:20,21; Jer 11:19; 18:18-20 Joh 11:47-53,57; Ac 4:25-28 the palace. 58; Jer 17:27; Mr 14:54 Caiaphas.This was Joseph, surnamed Caiaphas, who succeeded Simon son of Camith, in the high-priesthood, about A.D. 25. About two years after our Lord's death, he was deposed by Vitellius governor of Syria; and unable to bear his disgrace, and perhaps the stings of conscience for the murder of Christ, he killed himself about A.D. 35.</p>\n<p>Joh 11:49; 18:13,14,24; Ac 4:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-26-4","title":"Matthew 26:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":26,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":26,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>consulted. Ps 2:2 by. 23:33; Ge 3:1; Ac 7:19; 13:10; 2Co 11:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-26-5","title":"Matthew 26:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":26,"ve